duckdbsql Phase-1 qualification corpus

This directory contains short SQL inputs and provenance metadata used to
qualify the application-neutral parser and typed AST. Inputs are minimal
selection examples, not copied documentation or a replacement for DuckDB's
grammar. The corpus intentionally stores no serialized AST payloads.

Upstream provenance:

* DuckDB engine: https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb, commit
  08e34c447bae34eaee3723cac61f2878b6bdf787 (v1.5.4), MIT License.
* DuckDB documentation: https://github.com/duckdb/duckdb-web, commit
  0f4f64ac3c12c139edfd57947ceed142178c9419, MIT License.
* LeapSQL: https://github.com/leapstacklabs/leapsql, commit
  e6c4605252eac2aefe3cf502c9b156edee05a42d, Apache License 2.0.
* SQLGlot: https://github.com/tobymao/sqlglot, commit
  1ba7b2715dd9aba896edc7dc69fcc41bbb601b90d, MIT License.

The JSON manifest records each individual source path, commit, and license.
DuckDB remains the sole authority for generic parser behavior; the secondary
projects provide dialect-oriented examples only.
